# Rural Health Unit Management Information System (RHU MIS)
## Comprehensive System & Security Architecture Documentation

---

## 1. Executive Summary
The Rural Health Unit Management Information System (RHU MIS) is an enterprise-grade, web-based healthcare platform designed specifically to modernize, digitize, and secure the operational workflows of local government health units. Developed on the robust Laravel PHP framework, the system provides an end-to-end digital lifecycle for patient care—from online appointment booking and on-site triage, through clinical consultation, to laboratory diagnostics and pharmacy dispensing.

Crucially, the RHU MIS is engineered with a primary focus on data security, patient privacy, and clinical accountability, aligning with stringent international standards such as the **Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA)** and the **ISO/IEC 27001 Information Security Management System (ISMS)** standard.

---

## 2. System Architecture & Technological Stack

The system employs a Model-View-Controller (MVC) architectural pattern, ensuring a strict separation of concerns between data management, business logic, and user interface presentation.

- **Backend Framework:** Laravel 11.x (PHP 8.x)
- **Database Layer:** Relational Database (MySQL/MariaDB/SQLite) utilizing Eloquent ORM.
- **Frontend Stack:** 
  - Blade Templating Engine for server-side rendering.
  - Tailwind CSS for responsive, utility-first, consistent design aesthetics.
  - Alpine.js for lightweight, reactive frontend components (e.g., dynamic modals, real-time polling).
- **Asynchronous Processing:** Laravel Queues and background Jobs handle non-blocking operations like email dispatching.
- **Real-Time Simulation:** Alpine.js `setInterval` polling combined with Laravel `DatabaseNotifications` creates a robust, fallback-safe real-time alert system without the fragility of continuous WebSocket connections.

